• How the District’s data will be used, consistent with IC 33-133;
• How any user data collected will be analyzed, shared, or used and whether the provider can
  ensure the data is not used for AI model training;
• What kinds of data the provider keeps, how long it is kept, and who will have access to it;
• Measures they take to protect student and staff data; and
• Whether the tool complies with the requirements of the Children’s Online Privacy Protection Act
  (COPPA), the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (REPA), the Protection of Pupil Rights
  Amendment (PPRA), the Children’s Internet Protection Act (CIPA), the Individuals with
  Disabilities Education Act (IDEA), Title VI, Idaho student data privacy laws, and any Idaho AI
  legislation.

